  "scope": "Reconstruct selected frontier states from the original game and recorded chance-edge paths. Each path step must match its guarded state identity; raw history may differ within that existing quotient. At each frontier enumerate every legal target reply against the unchanged fixed opponent policy for one step. Replay hashes, path identities, legal-action products and chance mass are checked. Replace only these transitions, merge equal state/depth identities, sort by depth and recompute the full certificate with rational mass arithmetic and outward margins. Remaining leaves stay unknown. Both tied-upper reply rankings are retained for three adaptive rounds: reducing one maximizing branch need not reduce its parent if another branch ties. Ranking masses describe separate certificate paths and must not be added across rankings. Recorded certificate runs count its current transitions; additional replay/probe costs are reported separately. Fixed-opponent lower endpoints do not transfer to unrestricted security values; only upper bounds do. Engine transitions and guarded keys remain trusted. These are full-state first-action certificates, not blind guarantees, a whole-game solution or a bot change."
